  "goodToKnow": "Die Trauerfeier is a memorial or funeral service, held in a church, cemetery chapel or funeral home, followed by die Beisetzung or Beerdigung (burial). Afterwards, mourners often meet for coffee and cake or a meal, traditionally called der Leichenschmaus. Germans send Trauerkarten (condolence cards) and place Traueranzeigen (death notices) in newspapers. Die Trauer is grief. Plural: die Trauerfeiern."
